{"case_id": 1902, "Source": "Ukrainian corvette Vinnytsia", "Index": 11, "Text": "On 22 March 2014, following the annexation of Crimea by the Russian Federation, Vinnytsia was seized by Russian soldiers at her pier in the Southern Naval Base. Crimean separatist units lined up the crew and gave them the choice of remaining in Crimea and taking the oath of allegiance to the Republic of Crimea or leaving the peninsula. Half of the crew remained in Crimea, and on 19 April the corvette was towed to Odesa after Russia returned seized Ukrainian Navy ships. At Odesa, she became a training ship. By May 2016 the ship's complement numbered less than 30. Due to the need for major repairs and lack of spare parts for the ship, the Ukrainian Navy planned to decommission her in 2017, but the ship remained in service as of May 2016.", "entities": [{"entity": "22 March 2014", "label": "DATE", "start": 3, "end": 16, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Crimea", "label": "LOC", "start": 46, "end": 52, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Russian Federation", "label": "LOC", "start": 60, "end": 78, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "Vinnytsia", "label": "MISC", "start": 80, "end": 89, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "Russian", "label": "MISC", "start": 104, "end": 111, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Southern Naval Base", "label": "LOC", "start": 140, "end": 159, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Crimean", "label": "MISC", "start": 161, "end": 168, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "Crimea", "label": "LOC", "start": 245, "end": 251, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Republic of Crimea", "label": "LOC", "start": 293, "end": 311, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Crimea", "label": "LOC", "start": 367, "end": 373, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "19 April", "label": "DATE", "start": 382, "end": 390, "origin": "human_con