{"case_id": 5833, "Source": "Yevgeny Prigozhin", "Index": 33, "Text": "Prigozhin allegedly made personal efforts to establish contact with the presidential administration on the afternoon of 24 June 2023, including reaching out to Putin himself, who refused to speak with him. Final negotiations were reportedly conducted by Anton Vaino, the chief of staff, Nikolai Patrushev, the secretary of the Security Council, and Boris Gryzlov, the Russian ambassador to Belarus. Belarusian president Alexander Lukashenko reportedly spoke with Prigozhin upon Putin's request, acting as a mediator to broker a settlement. Charges were dropped and Wagner ceased its march on Moscow. As part of the agreement, Prigozhin moved to Belarus and Wagner troops were slated to return to Ukraine, but those plans were cancelled in the wake of Wagner's refusal to sign military contracts. Despite his charges being dropped, Prigozhin remained under investigation for treason.", "entities": [{"entity": "Prigozhin", "label": "PER", "start": 0, "end": 9, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "24 June 2023", "label": "DATE", "start": 120, "end": 132, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Putin", "label": "PER", "start": 160, "end": 165, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Anton Vaino", "label": "PER", "start": 254, "end": 265, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Nikolai Patrushev", "label": "PER", "start": 287, "end": 304, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Security Council", "label": "ORG", "start": 327, "end": 343, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Boris Gryzlov", "label": "PER", "start": 349, "end": 362, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Russian", "label": "MISC", "start": 368, "end": 375, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Belarus", "label": "LOC", "start": 390, "end": 397, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Belarusian", "label": "MISC", "start": 399, "end": 