{"case_id": 3092, "Source": "Kamianka Sich", "Index": 18, "Text": "In 1939 and 1953, archaeological excavations at the site were conducted by F. B. Kopylov and Olena Apanovych. As a result of the creation of the Kakhovka Reservoir and the erosion of its banks, by 1970 the condition of the Kamiaska Sich territory had significantly deteriorated: its entire southern and eastern parts had been destroyed. In 1972-73, an expedition of the Khortytsia State Historical and Cultural Reserve led by Oleksandr Bodiansky conducted research at the site. In 1974, extensive excavations were carried out by Arnold Sokulsky. This work was continued in 1989–91 by a joint expedition of the Institute of Archaeology of the National Academy of Sciences of Ukraine and the Khortytsia State Historical and Cultural Reserve under the leadership of A. O. Kozlovsky and V. E. Ilyinsky. Subsequently, in 2009, archaeological excavations were conducted under the direction of V. E. Ilyinsky. In 2011, D. D. Nikonenko conducted exploratory work to locate the remains of the Sich cemetery, but these searches were unsuccessful.", "entities": [{"entity": "1939", "label": "DATE", "start": 3, "end": 7, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "1953", "label": "DATE", "start": 12, "end": 16, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "F. B. Kopylov", "label": "PER", "start": 75, "end": 88, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Olena Apanovych", "label": "PER", "start": 93, "end": 108, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Kakhovka Reservoir", "label": "LOC", "start": 145, "end": 163, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "1970", "label": "DATE", "start": 197, "end": 201, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Kamiaska Sich", "label": "LOC", "start": 223, "end": 236, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "1972-73", "label": "DATE", "start": 340, "end": 347, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Khortytsia State His