{"case_id": 3357, "Source": "Slava-class cruiser", "Index": 4, "Text": "The Slava class was initially designated BLACKCOM 1 (Black Sea Combatant 1) and then designated the Krasina class for a short period until Slava was observed at sea. The SS-N-12 launchers are fixed facing forward at around 8° elevation with no reloads available. As there was nothing revolutionary about the design of the class, western observers felt they were created as a hedge against the failure of the more radical Kirov class. The helicopter hangar deck is located a half deck below the landing pad with a ramp connecting the two.", "entities": [{"entity": "Slava class", "label": "MISC", "start": 4, "end": 15, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "BLACKCOM 1", "label": "MISC", "start": 41, "end": 51, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Black Sea Combatant 1", "label": "MISC", "start": 53, "end": 74, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Krasina class", "label": "MISC", "start": 100, "end": 113, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Slava", "label": "MISC", "start": 139, "end": 144, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "SS-N-12", "label": "MISC", "start": 170, "end": 177, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Kirov class", "label": "MISC", "start": 421, "end": 432, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}], "entity_count": 7, "annotation_source": "full_paragraph_manual_review", "reviewed_at_utc": "2026-11-03T07:18:11.550847+00:00", "input_identity": "8c5e768a8c54b5c2cb3a33f357871fed75c4f2e056e36918105ee64acc580139", "rejected_flertdate_predictions": [], "baseline_predictions": [{"entity": "Slava class", "label": "MISC", "start": 4, "end": 15}, {"entity": "BLACKCOM 1", "label": "MISC", "start": 41, "end": 51}, {"entity": "Black Sea Combatant 1", "label": "MISC", "start": 53, "end": 74}, {"entity": "Krasina class", "label": "MISC", "start": 100, "end": 113}, {"entity": "Slava", "label": "MISC", "start": 139, "end":