{"case_id": 6315, "Source": "150th Guards Motor Rifle Division", "Index": 10, "Text": "The division was reformed at Turga in the Siberian Military District on July 23, 1942, based on the 1st Siberian Volunteer Division. The unit was made up of over 10,000 men from Siberian factories and the Kuzbass coal fields and had a cadre of 1,460 combat veterans. By September 1 it had enlisted 13,754 personnel, 43.8 percent of whom were Communist Party members or Komsomols. Within two weeks it was assigned to the 6th \"Siberian Volunteer\" Rifle Corps and began moving by rail to camps near Moscow where it received the last of its support troops and transport. On September 30, the 150th set out on a 170km road march to join the 22nd Army near Belyi, part of the Kalinin Front.", "entities": [{"entity": "Turga", "label": "LOC", "start": 29, "end": 34, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Siberian Military District", "label": "ORG", "start": 42, "end": 68, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "July 23, 1942", "label": "DATE", "start": 72, "end": 85, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "1st Siberian Volunteer Division", "label": "ORG", "start": 100, "end": 131, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Siberian", "label": "MISC", "start": 178, "end": 186, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "Kuzbass", "label": "LOC", "start": 205, "end": 212, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "September 1", "label": "DATE", "start": 270, "end": 281, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Communist Party", "label": "ORG", "start": 342, "end": 357, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "6th \"Siberian Volunteer\" Rifle Corps", "label": "ORG", "start": 420, "end": 456, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Moscow", "label": "LOC", "start": 496, "end": 502, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "September 30", "label": "DATE", "start": 570, "end": 582, "origin": "huma