{"case_id": 2032, "Source": "127th Motor Rifle Division (Russia)", "Index": 2, "Text": "The division formed part of the 35th Army of the Maritime Group of Forces in the Far East in May 1945. In August 1945 the division, as a part of 1st Far East Front, participated in the Soviet invasion of Manchuria. On 9 August 1945 the division began operations as part of 35th Army, advancing 12 kilometers, having forced the Songacha River in northern Heilongjiang. The division fought on the Ussuri River at Khotunsky (Хотунского), Mishan, Border (Пограничного), and Duninsky (Дунинского) fortified districts, capturing the cities of Mishan, Jilin, Jantszy, and Harbin. For its valour in combat and courage, the 66th Rifle Division was awarded the Order of Kutuzov, Second Degree, on 19 September 1945. Three Hero of the Soviet Union medals, 1266 awards, and 2838 medals were given to the division's personnel.", "entities": [{"entity": "35th Army", "label": "ORG", "start": 32, "end": 41, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Maritime Group of Forces", "label": "ORG", "start": 49, "end": 73, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Far East", "label": "LOC", "start": 81, "end": 89, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "May 1945", "label": "DATE", "start": 93, "end": 101, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "August 1945", "label": "DATE", "start": 106, "end": 117, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "1st Far East Front", "label": "ORG", "start": 145, "end": 163, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Soviet invasion of Manchuria", "label": "MISC", "start": 185, "end": 213, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "9 August 1945", "label": "DATE", "start": 218, "end": 231, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "35th Army", "label": "ORG", "start": 273, "end": 282, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Songacha River", "label": "LOC", "start": 327, "end": 341, "origin": "huma