{"case_id": 1066, "Source": "Russian strikes on religious sites during the invasion of Ukraine", "Index": 0, "Text": "During the Russian invasion of Ukraine, hundreds of religious buildings have been damaged or destroyed by missile, air, and drone attacks. According to UNESCO, at least 154 religious sites had been verified as damaged by June 2026, while Ukrainian government and religious-monitoring groups report much higher totals, exceeding 700 religious sites of various faiths. A January 2026 report by Mission Eurasia states that at least 737 religious buildings have been destroyed by Russian forces since the start of the full-scale invasion in 2022, including about 450 Baptist churches even though Baptists represent only 1-2% of the overall Ukrainian population. Besides churches, several mosques, synagogues, and other religious sites have also been attacked like the Sultan Suleiman Mosque in Mariupol that was affected by Russian shelling on 12 March 2022 despite sheltering more than 80 civilians including Turkish citizens.", "entities": [{"entity": "Russian invasion of Ukraine", "label": "MISC", "start": 11, "end": 38, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "UNESCO", "label": "ORG", "start": 152, "end": 158, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "June 2026", "label": "DATE", "start": 221, "end": 230, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Ukrainian", "label": "MISC", "start": 238, "end": 247, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "January 2026", "label": "DATE", "start": 369, "end": 381, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Mission Eurasia", "label": "ORG", "start": 392, "end": 407, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Russian", "label": "MISC", "start": 476, "end": 483, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "2022", "label": "DATE", "start": 537, "end": 541, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Baptist", "label": "MISC", "start": 563, "end": 570, "origin": 