{"case_id": 1893, "Source": "Ukrainian corvette Vinnytsia", "Index": 2, "Text": "The Grisha-class anti-submarine ships were designed to search for and destroy enemy submarines found in coastal areas. They were equipped with a variety of anti-submarine warfare (ASW) weapons. All were fitted with retractable fin stabilizers. The Grisha II class were modified variants built for the border guard between 1972 and 1983. These ships had a second 57-millimetre (2.2 in) gun mounting replacing the SA-N-4 missile system forward.", "entities": [{"entity": "Grisha-class", "label": "MISC", "start": 4, "end": 16, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Grisha II class", "label": "MISC", "start": 248, "end": 263, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "1972", "label": "DATE", "start": 322, "end": 326, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "1983", "label": "DATE", "start": 331, "end": 335, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "SA-N-4", "label": "MISC", "start": 412, "end": 418, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}], "entity_count": 5, "annotation_source": "full_paragraph_manual_review", "reviewed_at_utc": "2026-11-03T14:09:22.898393+00:00", "input_identity": "8c5e768a8c54b5c2cb3a33f357871fed75c4f2e056e36918105ee64acc580139", "rejected_flertdate_predictions": [], "baseline_predictions": [{"entity": "Grisha-class", "label": "MISC", "start": 4, "end": 16}, {"entity": "Grisha II class", "label": "MISC", "start": 248, "end": 263}, {"entity": "1972", "label": "DATE", "start": 322, "end": 326}, {"entity": "1983", "label": "DATE", "start": 331, "end": 335}, {"entity": "SA-N-4", "label": "MISC", "start": 412, "end": 418}], "history": []}
{"case_id": 6250, "Source": "Battle of Lysychansk", "Index": 5, "Text": "After the fall of Sievierodonetsk, Lysychansk became the last major city in the Luhansk Oblast under Ukrainian control. Military units of the separatist Luhansk People's Republic (LPR) fought alongside Russian infantry and were supported by Russian artillery and airstrikes. The Russian offensive against Lysychansk was overseen and planned by Aleksandr Lapin, Commander of the Central Military District, and Sergey Surovikin, Commander of the Russian Aerospace Forces. The Institute for the Study of War argued that the involvement of these top-level commanders showcased the importance Russian put into the city's capture. An initial Russian armored assault on Lysychansk was repelled by the pro-Ukrainian forces, with Belarusian volunteers under Ivan \"Brest\" Marchuk playing a major role in fighting off the tanks.", "entities": [{"entity": "Sievierodonetsk", "label": "LOC", "start": 18, "end": 33, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Lysychansk", "label": "LOC", "start": 35, "end": 45, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Luhansk Oblast", "label": "LOC", "start": 80, "end": 94, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Ukrainian", "label": "MISC", "start": 101, "end": 110, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Luhansk People's Republic", "label": "LOC", "start": 153, "end": 178, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "LPR", "label": "LOC", "start": 180, "end": 183, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "Russian", "label": "MISC", "start": 202, "end": 209, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Russian", "label": "MISC", "start": 241, "end": 248, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Russian", "label": "MISC", "start": 279, "end": 286, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Lysychansk", "label": "LOC", "start": 305, "end": 315, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Aleksan