{"case_id": 5541, "Source": "Palace \"Ukraine\"", "Index": 1, "Text": "It was opened in April 1970 as the biggest center of culture and arts. The building was primarily intended to serve as a venue for party congresses and events of the Communist Party of Ukraine, and secondarily as a concert hall. To construct it, Shelest the then party secretary of the Communist Party of Ukraine desguised the construction, in documents sent to Moscow, as only a concert hall. Reason for this was that the Palace had similar dimensions in scale as the Kremlin Palace of Congresses and would most likely not be approved. The building was designed by a group of architects P. Zhylytskyi, I. Vayner, under the directorship of the project's author the distinguished architect of Ukrainian SSR Yevheniya Marynchenko.", "entities": [{"entity": "April 1970", "label": "DATE", "start": 17, "end": 27, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Communist Party of Ukraine", "label": "ORG", "start": 166, "end": 192, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Shelest", "label": "PER", "start": 246, "end": 253, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Communist Party of Ukraine", "label": "ORG", "start": 286, "end": 312, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Moscow", "label": "LOC", "start": 362, "end": 368, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Kremlin Palace of Congresses", "label": "LOC", "start": 469, "end": 497, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "P. Zhylytskyi", "label": "PER", "start": 588, "end": 601, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "I. Vayner", "label": "PER", "start": 603, "end": 612, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Ukrainian SSR", "label": "LOC", "start": 692, "end": 705, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Yevheniya Marynchenko", "label": "PER", "start": 706, "end": 727, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}], "entity_count": 10, "annotation_source": "full_paragraph_