{"case_id": 4461, "Source": "Russian torture chambers in Ukraine", "Index": 5, "Text": "In July 2022, The Guardian reported on torture chambers in the Russian-occupied Zaporizhzhia region based on the testimony of a 16-year-old boy who was held in one of them beginning in April. The boy was arrested by Russian soldiers while trying to leave the occupied city of Melitopol because he had a video on his phone from social media, which featured Russian soldiers expressing defeatist attitudes towards Russia's invasion. He was held in a makeshift prison in Vasylivka. According to his testimony, he saw rooms where torture took place, as well as bloodstains and soaked bandages, and heard the screams of the people being tortured. The torture involved electric shocks and beating and could last for several hours.", "entities": [{"entity": "July 2022", "label": "DATE", "start": 3, "end": 12, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "The Guardian", "label": "ORG", "start": 14, "end": 26, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Russian-occupied", "label": "MISC", "start": 63, "end": 79, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "Zaporizhzhia", "label": "LOC", "start": 80, "end": 92, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "April", "label": "DATE", "start": 185, "end": 190, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "Russian", "label": "MISC", "start": 216, "end": 223, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Melitopol", "label": "LOC", "start": 276, "end": 285, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Russian", "label": "MISC", "start": 356, "end": 363, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Russia", "label": "LOC", "start": 412, "end": 418, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Vasylivka", "label": "LOC", "start": 468, "end": 477, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}], "entity_count": 10, "annotation_source": "full_paragraph_manual_review", "reviewed_at_utc": "2026-11-03T14:49:46.49