{"case_id": 2713, "Source": "Russian use of mobile crematoriums in Ukraine", "Index": 4, "Text": "On 6 April 2022, the Mariupol City Council accused Russia of using mobile crematoriums to burn the corpses of civilians to hide evidence of war crimes, writing \"[k]illers cover their tracks\". According to the Council, Russian authorities had \"ordered the destruction of any evidence of crimes committed by its army in Mariupol\" after the international outrage caused by the discovery of the Bucha atrocities. Mariupol Mayor Vadym Boychenko told the Associated Press in April that \"[m]obile crematoriums have arrived in the form of trucks: You open it, and there is a pipe inside and these bodies are burned\", stating he had several sources telling of methodical burning of corpses by Russian forces. Boychenko stated at that time the civilian death toll could surpass 20,000, accusing Russian forces of blocking humanitarian convoys to conceal the extent of casualties.", "entities": [{"entity": "6 April 2022", "label": "DATE", "start": 3, "end": 15, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Mariupol City Council", "label": "ORG", "start": 21, "end": 42, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Russia", "label": "LOC", "start": 51, "end": 57, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Council", "label": "ORG", "start": 209, "end": 216, "origin": "human_added_or_corrected"}, {"entity": "Russian", "label": "MISC", "start": 218, "end": 225, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Mariupol", "label": "LOC", "start": 318, "end": 326, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Bucha", "label": "LOC", "start": 391, "end": 396, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Mariupol", "label": "LOC", "start": 409, "end": 417, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Vadym Boychenko", "label": "PER", "start": 424, "end": 439, "origin": "human_confirmed_flertdate"}, {"entity": "Associated Press", "label": "ORG", "start":